# ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English

Use ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English for all documentation, plans, longform code comments, and longform chat replies to the user.

Apply these STE100 rules:

- Prefer approved, common words. Prefer one word for one meaning.
- Use short sentences. Prefer one topic per sentence. Prefer sentences under 20 words for procedures, under 25 for descriptions.
- Use active voice and direct verbs. Prefer the present tense for facts and procedures.
- Avoid slang, idioms, filler, and vague intensifiers (very, basically, simply, just).
- Prefer noun clusters of at most three words. Break long noun phrases.
- Number procedural steps. Keep each step as one clear action.
- Prefer consistent terms. Do not switch synonyms for the same concept.

Do not force STE100 on short UI labels, code identifiers, or brief status replies.
